In article <1fusduINN9u4@agate.berkeley.edu> werner@dewey.soe.berkeley.edu (John Werner) writes:

   In article <nwang.723699986@black.clarku.edu> nwang@black.clarku.edu (The freak) writes:
   >
   >My 1st level priest found a Wand of Wishing.  The first wish I think I
   >did the smart thing by wishing for a blessed scroll of charging, then
   >excalibur and gauntlets of power since he has strength of 9 and last
   >gray dragon scale mail.  So I have 3 wish left right?

   SPOILERS follow, of course.

   You do know that you're allowed to wish for 3 scrolls or potions?  So
   you could have wished for "3 belssed scrolls of charging" for example.
   On weapons and armor you can wish for a +3 bonus, i.e. "blessed +3 gray
   dragon scale mail."

   Cursed scrolls of genocide would probably be a waste at this point,
   where it's easy to get experience by killing things.  I usually don't
   use them until the character is above experience level 15 or so.  If
   you're really worried about hit points "3 blessed potions of gain
   ability" might help by raising constitution.  But I probably wouldn't
   do that either.

I disagree. The best game I ever had started in this way, and of
course I used the 3 cursed scrolls of genocide to get a level full of
nurses. That wound my max hit points up by about 100, without
increasing my character level and thus increasing the level of monster
that got created to bother me.

On top of that blessed +3 boots of speed and blessed +3 cloak of
invisibilty are probably what you want to keep you safe until much
later. Thus you can:-
(1) Fight a long time due to being hard to hit(invis) and hard to kill
(high max hp).
(2) Ignore monsters if you want (they can't find you when your invis
until much later in your career).
(3) Have free hits on tough monsters (cos of double speed)

You should be able to win from here.
